Differencing the log series to make it look stationary and reduce the variance. The ACF cuts off after lag 1 and the PACF decays (indicating a MA(1)). The PACF also shows seasonal spikes at lag 52, representing a seasonal AR(1) component.

# Models

## Model 1: seasonal ARIMA with trend

Let $y_t=\log(\text{crashes}_t)$ and $B$ the backshift operator. We fit

$$\Phi(B^{52})\,(1-B)\,(y_t-\delta t)=\Theta(B)\,\varepsilon_t,\qquad \varepsilon_t\sim N(0,\sigma^2)$$

- Chosen model: $\text{ARIMA}(0,1,1)(1,0,0)_{52}$ with a linear trend $\delta$.
- $\delta$ is the **weekly log growth rate**: the answer to our trend question.
- Annual % change $=100\,(e^{52.18\,\delta}-1)$.

## Model 2: state-space (local level + seasonal)

$$y_t = \underbrace{\mu_t}_{\text{level}} + \underbrace{s_t}_{\text{season}} + v_t,\quad v_t\sim N(0,R)$$

$$\mu_t=\mu_{t-1}+w_{1t},\qquad s_t=-\sum_{j=1}^{51}s_{t-j}+w_{2t}$$

- State vector $x_t=(\mu_t,s_t,\dots,s_{t-50})'$, with $x_t=\Phi x_{t-1}+w_t$ and $y_t=Ax_t+v_t$.
- Variances $(Q_{11},Q_{22},R)$ estimated by maximum likelihood via the Kalman filter; the trend is read from the Kalman **smoother**.

## ARIMA: search and diagnostics

```{r}
#| echo: true
fit2 <- total_ts |> model(
  auto = ARIMA(log(n_crashes) ~ trend() + pdq(0:3, 1, 0:3) + PDQ(0:2, 0, 0:2)),
  test = ARIMA(log(n_crashes) ~ trend() + pdq(0, 1, 1) + PDQ(1, 0, 0)))
glance(fit2) |> select(.model, AICc, BIC)
fit2 |> select(auto) |> report()
```

## ARIMA residuals

```{r}
fit2 |> select(test) |> gg_tsresiduals()
augment(fit2) |> filter(.model == "test") |>
  features(.innov, ljung_box, lag = 26, dof = 3)
```

